Progress: Completed round r3 landing review fixes for Featured Recognition (scene 4).

[featured.js](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-featured/public/color-polish/scenes/featured.js) now preserves the active expression ID during `keepAge` remounts and initializes `V.featuredAdvanced` from `sceneAge` so data refreshes do not trigger duplicate flips. `FEATURED_FLIP_CANCEL` aborts in-flight timers and animation listeners if remount happens during a flip. In [featured.css](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-featured/public/color-polish/scenes/featured.css), `overflow: hidden` was removed from `.feature-panel` and moved to a dedicated `.feature-sweep-clip` wrapper, keeping light sweeps bounded while preserving 3D transform depth for the medallion, rings, and orbit.

### What works now
- Remounting with `keepAge: true` preserves `FEATURED_PASS_ID` when `sceneAge > 0.5` rather than drawing a new ID.
- `V.featuredAdvanced` initializes to `S.sceneAge >= 15`, preventing immediate secondary flips after remounts.
- `FEATURED_FLIP_CANCEL` cleanly clears timeouts and detaches animation listeners if a flip was in progress during remount.
- `.feature-panel` retains `transform-style: preserve-3d` without being flattened by overflow clipping.
- Three unread `V.featuredId` assignments were removed.
- [featured.spec.ts](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-featured/tests/color-polish-scenes/featured.spec.ts) includes automated tests covering `keepAge` remount stability and 3D sweep-clip structure.
